    "md5": "0349025a345e5a3d4011c335b7c0a9aa",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1927,
    "chunk_text": "Paw-Sperity \u00a0Xtravaganza: A day out for whole family on 29 March\n\nThe Paw-Sperity Xtravaganza, to be held on 29 March at the Cinnamon Grand, in aid of Rescue Animals Sri Lanka (RAS), promises to be a day filled with fun, good food, shopping and entertainment, one that\u00a0 ushers\u00a0 in Avurudu Cheer as well as Easter Joy.\n\nThis year Browns Veterinary\u00a0 Pharmaceuticals have come on board to partner with RAS, while a Kiddies play area, run by the ABC Group of Schools with both indoor handicrafts and an outdoor play area, will keep your little ones fully entertained while you shop till you drop. A traditional welcome by none other than the Easter Bunny and the Village Headman, Rabban players, Kavum Ammes, a staggering selection of exciting goodies from over 50 stalls, perfect for gift-giving and personal indulgence, makes Paw-Sperity a treat for the entire family , with\u00a0 tradition combining good cheer, and all for a worthy cause \u2014Animal Welfare.\n\nThis year sees a departure from tradition, as instead of one particular Chief Guest, RAS will recognize a\u00a0 number of their supporters and well-wishers who have helped them over the years,\u00a0 all of whom will light the oil lamp and declare the opening of the Bazaar. Paw-Sperity which actually combines the words paw and prosperity, symbolize\u00a0 what this event is all about \u2013 animal welfare and prosperity for all. What\u2019s more,\u00a0 Little Jax, a miniature Dachshund who is the RAS mascot, will also be present to light the oil lamp, all dressed up for the occasion in a batik sarong , gifted to him,\u00a0 from well-known Batik Brand CHERUB.\n\nAnother heartwarming feature of this year\u2019s Paw-Sperity\u00a0 Xtravaganza will be the presence of children from the Indira Cancer Trust who will be treated to games and handicrafts at the Kiddies Play Area. It is hoped that as many children who are in the recovery stages will be present to enjoy some Avurudu cheer and Easter joy."
  },
