    "chunk_size_bytes": 1757,
    "chunk_text": "Let me commence  by re-visiting the previous Tamil Nadu state election held in 2021.Since 1967  Tamil Nadu state  has been ruled by political parties subscribing to what is termed as Dravidian ideology. Either the Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam (DMK) or its alternative the All India Anna-Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam (AIADMK) have been enjoying power in the State alternately.\n\nAt the 2021 poll,the DMK led Secular Progressive Alliance (SPA) won 159 seats while the AIADMK led National Democratic Alliance (NDA) won 75. No other party or alliance won even a single seat.  The Naam Thamizhar Katchi (NTK) led by cinema director cum actor S. Seemaan contested all 234 seats and came third by polling over three million votes even though it failed to get an MLA elected.\n\nNominations for the 2026 elections  will close on April 7th 2026.  Details of the electorates contested by various political parties and the candidates fielded by them would be officially known only then. A detailed incisive analysis would be possible only after that.\n\nHowever a preliminary overview indicates that the 2026  poll would be mainly on the lines of the 2021 election. The  Tamil Nadu election is very much likely be a battle between the DMK led SPA alliance and the AIADMK led NDA alliance. Yet the election is termed by  several  observers  as a four cornered fight because two other parties are also contesting  all 234 seats separately. One is the NTK led by Seemaan and the other is the TVK led by Vijay.\n\nSome analysts view the election as a triangular tussle between the DMK led alliance,the AIADMK alliance and Vijay\u2019s TVK. Seemaan\u2019s NTK is not taken into account by these analysts despite the fact that the party polled 8% of the votes ib the  2021 poll and came third."
