    "chunk_size_bytes": 1837,
    "chunk_text": "The fact that a leading actor like Vijay could launch his own political party and aspire to be the future chief minister of Tamil Nadu is mainly due to the \u201ccinematic politics\u201d ecosystem prevailing in the state.\n\nAccording to knowledgeable political observers Vijay\u2019s TVK draws its support mainly from youths who are below 35. There is  much woman support also. In terms of area, Vijay\u2019s support is more in urban areas than rural areas. The TVP is expected  to do well in the state capital Chennai as well as other Tamil Nadu cities.\n\nOn another level  Vijay is expected to get substantial support from the Vellala community, scheduled castes,linguistic minorities  and the religious  minorities. Vijay himself is a Vellala Christian.\n\nBoth the DMK and AIADMK form  multi-party alliances to contest elections. However after winning,they form a single party administration. Electoral allies are not given ministerial portfolios. This has led to some rumblings of discontent among other parties.\n\nWhen Vijay launched his Party,he invited other political parties to align with him. Vijay promised them a share in power and Governance.In short , electoral allies would be given minister posts. Negotiations were conducted quietly with many political parties except the ruling DMK.This was because Vijay was positioning his TVK as the alternative to the DMK. Despite  offering minister posts,no Tamil Nadu party was willing to climb aboard Vijay\u2019s bandwagon.\n\nThis reportedly was due to two reasons. One was that political parties were not willing to throw in their lot with the untested,unproven new kid on the block. The second was Vijay\u2019s insistence that he alone should be the chief minster. Unable to secure any ally, Vijay made a virtue of necessity by announcing last week that the party would go it alone at the elections."
